From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tell genccode the CPU architecture under clang-cl

Backport of nodejs/node#64263 ("build: fix Windows small-icu build with
ClangCL"), which is not in 26.6.0.

ICU's genccode writes the data file straight to a COFF object on
Windows, and when it was itself compiled by clang it refuses to guess
the machine type from its own predefined macros -- the tool runs on the
host and may be producing an object for another architecture -- so it
insists on -c <arch>:

  genccode: CPU architecture must be set for Clang-CL

The small-icu action for Windows did not pass one.  node's own Windows
builds are full-icu, which takes a different path, so the small-icu
build was broken there from the moment clang-cl became the compiler.
---
 tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp b/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
--- a/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
+++ b/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
@@ -228,6 +228,7 @@
                   'outputs': [ '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/icudt<(icu_ver_major)<(icu_endianness)_dat.<(icu_asm_ext)' ],
                   'action': [ '<(PRODUCT_DIR)/genccode<(EXECUTABLE_SUFFIX)',
                               '<@(icu_asm_opts)', # -o
+                              '-c', '<(target_arch)',
                               '-d', '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/',
                               '-n', 'icudata',
                               '-e', 'icusmdt<(icu_ver_major)',
